        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.084,
            0.744,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": "Some plants are not as tall as trees. These plants often have many brown woody stems that start branching very close to the ground. These stems are hard but not as thick as the stem of a tree. These plants are called **shrubs**. For example, a rose plant is a shrub (Fig. 2.3b)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.183,
            0.743,
            0.242
          ],
          "content": "Some plants are typically small with soft and green stems. These are known as **herbs**. For example, a tomato plant is a herb (Fig. 2.3c)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.242,
            0.743,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": "Some plants with weak stems need support to climb and grow, and are called **climbers**. Some plants creep along the ground and are called **creepers**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.302,
            0.743,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": "What can be other features on the basis of which you can group plants? Let us perform another activity."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.349,
            0.421,
            0.37
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 2.5: Let us compare"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.379,
            0.743,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": "Look at the leaves of different plants collected by you, during the nature walk."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.426,
            0.743,
            0.466
          ],
          "content": " Do you notice any variation in the shape and structure of these leaves?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.472,
            0.744,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "You may observe thin lines on the leaves of the plants (Fig. 2.4a). These are **veins**. The pattern of veins on the leaf is called **venation**. What differences do you see in the veins of leaves shown in Fig. 2.4a and Fig. 2.4b?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.58,
            0.256,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.123,
                0.682,
                0.295,
                0.714
              ],
              "content": "(a) Hibiscus leaf with reticulate venation"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
