                0.6,
                0.682,
                0.747,
                0.715
              ],
              "content": "(c) Grass leaf with parallel venation"
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.724,
            0.646,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 2.4: Leaves showing different types of venation"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.747,
            0.745,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": "In some leaves, you can observe a net-like pattern of veins on both sides of a thick middle vein. This pattern is called **reticulate venation**. For example, leaves of hibiscus exhibit reticulate venation (Fig. 2.4a). In some leaves, you may observe that the veins run parallel. This pattern is called **parallel venation**. For example, the leaves of banana plants and grasses exhibit parallel venation (Fig. 2.4b and Fig. 2.4c)."
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
